From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:51:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add homepage event-discovery sections
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds Popular Events, Recommended for You, Trending Events Near {city},
and one 5-event Concerts/Sports/Theater/Comedy row each to the homepage.

Backend: new GET /api/events/discover endpoint. Popularity/trending are
derived from real click_events data (all-time and last-7-days counts);
Recommended for You uses a popularity + recency + category-diversity
scoring pass (with a small boost for categories the visitor has actually
clicked into this session, tracked client-side) since the site has no
login/account system to draw real preferences from yet. Every section
backfills with the soonest nearby upcoming events when there isn't yet
enough click data to fill 5 slots, and each category section runs its
own dedicated query so a thin shared candidate pool never shorts one
category.

Frontend: visitor location for these sections comes from a ZIP code the
visitor can type in (resolved via zippopotam.us — no API key needed) or,
failing that, browser geolocation reverse-geocoded to a city name (via
bigdatacloud's free reverse-geocode API) — city name is required for the
"Trending Events Near {city}" heading, which the ZIP lookup gives
directly. Extracted the existing event-card markup into a shared
EventCard component (was duplicated inline in the main grid) plus a new
EventSection row component, reused by all seven new sections and the
existing "Featured Events" grid.

